+// step — to its current position, and resolves the FIRST contact. Tunnelling
+// is discrete-position blindness: at level 6 a stuttered frame moves the ball
+// 35.5 px against 34 px to cross a brick (`BRICK_H` + diameter), so sampling
+// only before/after the move would jump straight over it.
+//
+// The grid gap (`BRICK_GAP` = 8 px) is narrower than the ball's diameter
+// (14 px), so a seam overlaps TWO bricks in the same pass: only ONE bounce is
+// applied per step, otherwise `vy = -vy` applied twice cancels out and the
